# Trust Tasks — code ownership
#
# Each Trust Task specification lives in specs/<slug>/<version>/.
# Slugs may be hierarchical (multiple path segments separated by /),
# in which case the on-disk folder matches the slug (e.g. specs/acl/grant/).
# The release-critical paths — CI and the publish workflows, the release and
# bump scripts, the release and changelog configuration, the workspace manifest
# and the toolchain pin — are owned by the DTGWG admins team (#1144), so a change
# to what ships, or how, requests review from more than one person. Everything
# else requests one maintainer's review rather than routing review per
# namespace. The per-namespace rules below are where a namespace's own editors
# go once they exist: give a namespace an owner by appending a rule for its slug
# or slug prefix naming that team or individual.
#
# This file only requests review. The branch rules require none (approvals 0,
# code-owner review off), so a request here does not block a merge.
#
# Nothing else reads this file: the website's spec authors come from each
# spec's front matter or its folder's git history, not from here.

# Default — anything not matched below
*                                  @stormer78

# Framework material
/SPEC.md                           @stormer78
/CONTRIBUTING.md                   @stormer78
/CONTRIBUTING-SPECS.md             @stormer78
/LICENSE.md                        @stormer78
/SOURCE_CODE.md                    @stormer78
/README.md                         @stormer78

# Release-critical: CI and the publish workflows, release and bump scripts,
# release/changelog/licence configuration, the workspace manifest and lockfile,
# the toolchain pin. A team, so review is not one person's.
/.github/                          @trustoverip/dtgwg-admins
/scripts/                          @trustoverip/dtgwg-admins
/release-plz.toml                  @trustoverip/dtgwg-admins
/cliff.toml                        @trustoverip/dtgwg-admins
/deny.toml                         @trustoverip/dtgwg-admins
/Cargo.toml                        @trustoverip/dtgwg-admins
/Cargo.lock                        @trustoverip/dtgwg-admins
/rust-toolchain.toml               @trustoverip/dtgwg-admins
/package.json                      @trustoverip/dtgwg-admins
/package-lock.json                 @trustoverip/dtgwg-admins
/infra/                            @trustoverip/dtgwg-admins
/specs/spec.meta.schema.json       @stormer78

# Website chrome (everything except the auto-synced specs/ tree)
/website/                          @stormer78
/website/specs/                    # generated by scripts/build-registry.mjs — no owner override needed

# Individual Trust Task namespaces — one rule per top-level slug segment.
# Replace @stormer78 with the editorial team for that namespace once it exists.
# A rule on /specs/acl/ covers every spec under that prefix
# (acl/grant, acl/revoke, acl/change-role, acl/list, acl/show).
/specs/acl/                        @stormer78

# Peer-to-peer relationship credentials and the witnessing that can accompany
# them — authored jointly with the DTG Core Credentials task force (see #173).
/specs/vrc/                        @stormer78
/specs/witness/                    @stormer78

# Framework-reserved response types: registry-published implementations
# of the slugs reserved by SPEC §6.1. Framework editors only.
/specs/trust-task-error/           @stormer78
/specs/trust-task-ok/              @stormer78
/specs/trust-task-next-step/       @stormer78

